    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363-a6">

                <pb facs="0735" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg625"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 211.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ryan to Mr.
                            King.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 18,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Kindly advise me by earliest mail of the
                    present status of the case of R. C. Work, and what action, if any, is desired to
                    secure a final trial, so as to promote justice.</p>
                <p>I wrote on August 15 last asking for information regarding the alleged
                    suppression by the court of the testimony of the two Vega boys, but have no
                    reply from you. Be kind enough to inform me thereon; also what each will swear
                    to.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. Ryan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
